es, height in meters/feet, and key facts (Updated 2026)","image":"","datePublished":"2026-08-16T18:15:00.000000Z","dateModified":"2026-08-27T07:22:55.000000Z","author":[{"@type":"Person","name":"Admin","url":"https://www.nepalhikingteam.com/author/admin","image":"https://nht-api.nepalhikingteam.com/media/blog/author/admin.jpg"}],"publisher":{"@id":"https://www.nepalhikingteam.com/#organization"},"mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.nepalhikingteam.com/where-is-mount-everest"},"speakable":{"@type":"SpeakableSpecification","cssSelector":[".article-title"]},"wordCount":5334,"timeRequired":"PT27M","articleSection":"Travel Tips","keywords":"Where is Mount Everest, Highest peak in the world, Mount Everest Height, Location of Mount Everest, Everest result, Mount EVerest Location, Which country in Everest"}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is Mount Everest known for worldwide?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Mount Everest is known worldwide as the highest mountain on Earth, a symbol of extreme mountaineering, and a culturally sacred peak."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who named Everest?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The name Everest was named by Sir Andrew Waugh, a British officer (Surveyor General of India), in honor of his predecessor, Sir George Everest. Mount Everest was officially named by the Royal Geographical Society in 1865. The name was proposed by British Surveyor General of India, Andrew Scott Waugh, to honor his predecessor, Sir George Everest."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Mount Everest still growing?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, the world's highest point is still growing by approximately 4 mm every year due to the ongoing collision of the Indian and Eurasian tectonic plates; this tectonic activity was started thousands and millions of years ago. Mount Everest is still growing taller. It currently rises by about 2 to 4 millimeters (0.1 to 0.15 inches) each year."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many people have climbed Mount Everest and survived?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Over 7,500 unique individuals have successfully climbed Mount Everest and survived their expeditions, completing over 13,700 total ascents. Because many mountaineers (particularly local Sherpa guides) climb the peak multiple times, the total count of individual survivors is lower than the overall number of summits."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How high is Mount Everest? Height above sea level","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Mount Everest is 8,848.86 meters (29,031.7 feet) tall above sea level, making it the highest mountain on Earth. The measurement was made by a joint effort by Nepal and China in 2020."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Mont Everest: What are the facts of Mt. Everest?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Everest is growing every year by approximately 4mm, which is about 0.16 inches. It grows annually due to the movements of the tectonic plate.Mt. Everest is not a political feature but a purely true physical feature, a natural landform despite straddling between Nepal and Tibet.A native people of Everest region are Sherpa, who are renowned for their dexterity in climbing and also play a significant role in guiding expeditions. Their work, courage, and kindness make them the unsung heroes of Everest.Everyone is familiar with the famous trekkers Tenzing Norgay and Sir Edmund Hillary, who were the first to reach the mighty Mount Everest successfully. However, there are a lot of untold stories behind, particularly of those courageous Sherpas and other unsung heroes of Everest who laid the groundwork with their sacrifices, resilience, and tremendous support for this iconic achievement.Everest Base Camp is not the highest point of Everest. It is just the foothill of Everest, located well below, nearly 3,000m down from its peak.Above 8,000m lies the \"Death Zone.\" It is called so because of a lack of oxygen, the freezing temperature, and unpredictable climate that make survival a true test of human tolerance."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where is Mount Everest located on the world map? Which country Mt. Everest is in? Where do we find Everest?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The world's tallest mountain, the Mt. Everest, is located in Himalayas in South Asia, standing astride between two international borders, Nepal and its neighboring country, Tibet Autonomous Region of China. Everest Dağı nerede: The peak of Mt. Everest is situated in Asia and is considered the world's highest mountain by the globe, with a soaring height of exactly 8,848.86 meters / 29,031.7 feet."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Mount Everest a Physical feature?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Everest is a physical feature, not a political one, as it is a natural landform formed by the huge ancient collision of the two tectonic plates. Even though it straddles the political boundary between Nepal and Tibet (China), it is not a political pawn to be pushed about on maps since it is not man-made or governed by human-defined boundaries."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What continent is Mount Everest on? Mt Everest Where is it and Which Continent","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Mount Everest is located in the continent of Asia, specifically on the border between Nepal and the Tibet Autonomous Region of China, within the Himalayas."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Berg Everest: What is Berg Everest? Where is Berg Everest?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"&ldquo;Berg Everest&rdquo; simply means &ldquo;Mount Everest&rdquo; in German.&ldquo;Berg&rdquo; = mountain&ldquo;Everest&rdquo; = the name of the mountainSo, when someone says &ldquo;Berg Everest,&rdquo; they are referring to Mount Everest, the world&rsquo;s highest mountain, which stands at 8,848.86 meters (29,031.7 ft) above sea level."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Mount Everest in Pakistan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No, Mount Everest is not in Pakistan. It is located in the Mahalangur Himal sub-range of the Himalayas, exactly on the international border between Nepal and the Tibet Autonomous Region of China."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where is Mount Everest in Asia?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Mount Everest is located in the Himalayas, a mountain range in Asia. Specifically, it straddles the border between Nepal and the Tibet Autonomous Region of China. The mountain's location is defined by the Mahalangur sub-range of the Himalayas."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where is Mount Everest in multiple languages","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Hindi &ndash; माउंट एवरेस्ट नेपाल और चीन के तिब्बत स्वायत्त क्षेत्र की सीमा पर स्थित है।Bengali &ndash; মাউন্ট এভারেস্ট নেপাল ও চীনের তিব্বত স্বায়ত্তশাসিত অঞ্চলের সীমান্তে অবস্থিত।Tamil &ndash; எவரெஸ்ட் மலை நேபாளம் மற்றும் சீனாவின் திபெத் தன்னாட்சி பிரதேச எல்லையில் உள்ளது.Telugu &ndash; మౌంట్ ఎవరెస్ట్ నేపాల్ మరియు చైనా టిబెట్ స్వయంపాలిత ప్రాంత సరిహద్దులో ఉంది.Marathi &ndash; माउंट एव्हरेस्ट नेपाळ आणि चीनच्या तिबेट स्वायत्त प्रदेशाच्या सीमेवर आहे।Gujarati &ndash; માઉન્ટ એવરેસ્ટ નેપાળ અને ચીનની તિબ્બત સ્વાયત્ત પ્રદેશની સરહદે આવેલું છે।Punjabi &ndash; ਮਾਊਂਟ ਐਵਰੇਸਟ ਨੇਪਾਲ ਅਤੇ ਚੀਨ ਦੇ ਤਿਬਤ ਖੇਤਰ ਦੀ ਸਰਹੱਦ &rsquo;ਤੇ ਸਥਿਤ ਹੈ।Portuguese &ndash; O monte Evereste est&aacute; situado na fronteira entre o Nepal e a Regi&atilde;o Aut&oacute;noma do Tibete, na China.🇵🇱 Poland (Polish) - Mount Everest znajduje się na granicy Nepalu i Autonomicznego Regionu Tybetu w Chinach.🇩🇰 Denmark (Danish) - Mount Everest ligger p&aring; gr&aelig;nsen mellem Nepal og Kinas autonome region Tibet.Germany: Wo liegt der Mount Everest?🇵🇭 Philippines (Filipino/Tagalog): Tagalog &ndash; Ang Bundok Everest ay matatagpuan sa hangganan ng Nepal at Rehiyong Awtonomo ng Tibet sa Tsina.(Optional in English, which is also widely spoken in the Philippines) Mount Everest is located on the border between Nepal and China&rsquo;s Tibet Autonomous Region."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Mt Everest located in what country: What country is Mt Everest in","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Mount Everest is located on the border between two countries: Nepal and China. The summit of Mount Everest sits precisely on the international border, with the north side in the Tibet Autonomous Region of China and the south side in Nepal."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What city is close to Mount Everest?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The nearest significant town to Mount Everest is Lukla, Nepal, which serves as the main entry point for trekkers and climbers heading to Everest Base Camp. The capital city of Kathmandu is also relatively close, about 160 km southwest of Everest and is the usual starting point for trips to the region."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Mount Everest in both Nepal and Tibet?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, Mount Everest is located on the border of Nepal and the Tibet Autonomous Region of China. The summit of Mount Everest straddles the international border, with its north face in Tibet and its south face in Nepal."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you get to Everest from Tibet?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, you can absolutely get to Mount Everest from Tibet, which is home to the Qomolangma Base Camp (the Chinese side of Everest Base Camp). Travelers can drive to the base camp, offering a direct and convenient way to see the mountain, though there are also trekking and even advanced climbing routes available from the Tibetan side."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which country does Mount Everest belong to?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Mount Everest belongs to both Nepal and China, as it sits directly on the international border between the two countries. The summit is the exact border, with the southern side in Nepal and the northern side in the Tibet Autonomous Region of China."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which country is the owner of Mount Everest? Who does Everest belong to?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Mount Everest is not owned by a single country; it sits on the border between Nepal and China, with the southern slopes in Nepal and the northern slopes in China's Tibet Autonomous Region. The summit itself is on the international border, making it a shared natural wonder and border mountain between the two nations."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where is my Mount Everest located?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"My Mount Everest is located on the border between Nepal and China (Tibet Autonomous Region), within the Mahalangur Himal mountain range of the Himalayas, with coordinates approximately 27.9881&deg; N latitude and 86.9250&deg; E longitude. The mountain's summit lies directly on this international border, with the southern side in Nepal and the northern side in Tibet."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Mount Everest be located in India?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No, Mount Everest is not located in India; it sits on the border between Nepal and China (Tibet Autonomous Region). While India was involved in early surveys and its tectonic plates are responsible for the Himalayas' formation, Mount Everest's summit is located in Nepal and Tibet."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which country is close to Mount Everest?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Mount Everest is on the border of two countries, Nepal and China. The summit of the mountain sits on the international border, with the southern side in Nepal and the northern side in Tibet, which is a region of China."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are there really sea fossils on top of Mount Everest?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, marine fossils such as shells and sea lilies have been discovered high on Mount Everest. These fossils are found in limestone layers known as the &ldquo;Qomolangma Formation,&rdquo; which forms the summit pyramid of Mount Everest. The rock was once part of the ancient Tethys Sea more than 400 million years ago, long before the Himalayas existed. Over millions of years, the collision between the Indian and Eurasian tectonic plates pushed this former seabed upward, eventually raising it to what we now call the Roof of the World."}}]}</script><section class="banner block relative page-banner after:bg-wave after:bottom-0 after:rotate-180 after:z-10 after:bg-transparent after:bg-left after:bg-repeat-x after:bg-cover after:h-5 after:left-0 after:right-0 after:absolute"><div class="intro-image relative after:absolute after:inset-0 after:bg-black/10 after:z-10"><figure class="bg-stretch image-slot before:pt-[67.47%] md:before:pt-[46.0625%] lg:before:pt-[39.0625%]"><img alt="Where is Mount Everest" fetchPriority="high" width="1650" height="645" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="object-cover" style="color:transparent" sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, (max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1650px" srcSet="/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnht-api.nepalhikingteam.com%2Fmedia%2Fblog%2Fbanner%2Fwhere-is-mount-everest-1735280233.jpg&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnht-api.nepalhikingteam.com%2Fmedia%2Fblog%2Fbanner%2Fwhere-is-mount-everest-1735280233.jpg&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnht-api.nepalhikingteam.com%2Fmedia%2Fblog%2Fbanner%2Fwhere-is-mount-everest-1735280233.jpg&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnht-api.nepalhikingteam.com%2Fmedia%2Fblog%2Fbanner%2Fwhere-is-mount-everest-1735280233.jpg&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnht-api.nepalhikingteam.com%2Fmedia%2Fblog%2Fbanner%2Fwhere-is-mount-everest-1735280233.jpg&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnht-api.nepalhikingteam.com%2Fmedia%2Fblog%2Fbanner%2Fwhere-is-mount-everest-1735280233.jpg&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnht-api.nepalhikingteam.com%2Fmedia%2Fblog%2Fbanner%2Fwhere-is-mount-everest-1735280233.jpg&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnht-api.nepalhikingteam.com%2Fmedia%2Fblog%2Fbanner%2Fwhere-is-mount-everest-1735280233.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnht-api.nepalhikingteam.com%2Fmedia%2Fblog%2Fbanner%2Fwhere-is-mount-everest-1735280233.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75"/></figure></div><div class="banner-caption absolute inset-x-0 bottom-[10%] z-20 drop-shadow-md"><div class="container"><div class="lg:w-9/12 mx-auto"><blockquote class=" text-white font-bold text-lg text-left md:text-xl lg:text-2xl">Mount Everest 8848.86 m</blockquote></div></div></div></section><main class="common-box blog-page pt-0" role="main" itemScope="" itemType="https://schema.org/Blog"><div class="content container"><div class="page-title flex flex-wrap gap-y-3 gap-x-8 justify-between"><div class="lg:max-w-[calc(100%_-_390px)]"><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb"><nav class="breadcrumb-nav font-secondary hidden md:block relative z-10 mb-3" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol class="breadcrumb flex items-center text-xxs font-medium text-muted [&amp;&gt;li&gt;a]:inline-block [&amp;&gt;li&gt;a]:leading-[1.5]"><li class="breadcrumb-item"><a class="text-muted underline hover:text-primary" href="/">Home</a></li><li class="breadcrumb-item"><a class="text-muted hover:text-secondary" href="/blog">Blog</a></li><li class="breadcrumb-item"><a class="text-muted hover:text-secondary" href="/travel-tips">Travel Tips</a></li><li class="breadcrumb-item active"><span class="text-secondary">Where is Mount Everest Located? Country, Location &amp; Height</span></li></ol></nav></nav><h1 class="article-title">Where is Mount Everest Located? Country, Location &amp; Height</h1></div><aside class="blog-meta-sidebar"><div class="blog-meta xl:max-w-[350px] flex items-center text-right flex-row-reverse text-xs font-medium"><div class="avatar flex-[0_0_50px] h-[50px] w-[50px] border border-secondary rounded-full"><img alt="Admin - Author profile picture" loading="lazy" width="53" height="53" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="rounded-full" style="color:transparent" srcSet="/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnht-api.nepalhikingteam.com%2Fmedia%2Fblog%2Fauthor%2Fadmin.jpg&amp;w=64&amp;q=75 1x, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnht-api.nepalhikingteam.com%2Fmedia%2Fblog%2Fauthor%2Fadmin.jpg&amp;w=128&amp;q=75 2x" src="/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnht-api.nepalhikingteam.com%2Fmedia%2Fblog%2Fauthor%2Fadmin.jpg&amp;w=128&amp;q=75"/></div><div class="meta-dtl text-muted text-xxs pr-[15px] font-medium"><a class="block text-secondary mb-1 pb-1 font-medium border-b border-secondary text-[.9375rem]" rel="author" aria-label="View more articles by Admin" href="https://www.nepalhikingteam.com/author/admin">Admin</a><div class="meta-info flex flex-wrap justify-end gap-x-1.5 text-xs"><time dateTime="2026-08-27T07:22:55.000000Z" class="date" title="Last updated: 27th Aug 2026" itemProp="dateModified">Updated: <!-- -->27th Aug 2026</time><span class="reading-time" aria-label="Estimated reading time" itemProp="timeRequired">  |  <!-- -->27 min read</span><div class="categories" role="navigation" aria-label="Article categories">  |  <a class="category-link" rel="category tag" aria-label="View more articles in Travel Tips category" href="https://www.nepalhikingteam.com/travel-tips">Travel Tips</a></div></div></div></div></aside></div><div class="package-container"><div class="package-container-left"><article class="common-module blog-detail [&amp;_blockquote]:mb-6 [&amp;_blockquote]:text-[1.125rem] [&amp;_h2]:scroll-mt-24 [&amp;_h3]:scroll-mt-24" id="blog-detail" itemScope="" itemType="https://schema.org/BlogPosting"><p>Mount Everest (known locally as Sagarmāthā in Nepal and Qomolangma in Tibet) is the highest point on Earth, reaching an official elevation of 8,848.86 meters (29,031.7 feet). Mount Everest is located in the Himalayan mountain range in Asia. Nepal and China jointly measured and announced this updated height, ending years of small differences in official records. Located in the Mahalangur Himal sub-range of the Himalayas on the China-Nepal border, it is a premier destination for both extreme mountaineers and recreational trekkers.</p>
<p><strong>Mount Everest is located on the international border between Nepal (to the south) and Tibet (China), within the Mahalangur sub-range of the Himalayas.</strong> Mount <strong>everest is not in India &amp; Pakistan and it is true</strong>. It stands on the Tibetan Plateau and is a shared natural wonder between these two regions, with the summit sitting precisely on the international border. On the Nepalese side, Mt Everest is located in the Solukhumbu District and Sagarmatha National Park, while on the Chinese side, it is in the Tingri County of the Tibetan Plateau.</p>
<div class="responsive-table">
<table style="width: 100.03%; height: 512px;"><caption><strong><em>Everest Where is Mount Everest Located? Find out in Detail</em></strong></caption>
<tbody>
<tr style="height: 35.2px;">
<td style="width: 18.5594%;"><strong>Mountain Name</strong></td>
<td style="width: 79.506%;"><strong>Mount Everest is in which country</strong></td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 57.6px;">
<td style="width: 18.5594%;"><strong>Local Name of Mount Everest</strong></td>
<td style="width: 79.506%;">Sagarmatha, which means "Forehead of the Sky<br>Chomolungma (or Qomolangma), meaning "Goddess Mother of the World.</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 35.2px;">
<td style="width: 18.5594%;"><strong>Continent</strong></td>
<td style="width: 79.506%;">Asia</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 35.2px;">
<td style="width: 18.5594%;"><strong>Mountain Range of Mt Everest</strong></td>
<td style="width: 79.506%;">Himalayas</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 35.2px;">
<td style="width: 18.5594%;"><strong>Significance</strong></td>
<td style="width: 79.506%;">Highest mountain in the world</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 35.2px;">
<td style="width: 18.5594%;"><strong>Specific Range</strong></td>
<td style="width: 79.506%;">Mahalangur Himal (or Mahalangur Range, sub-range of the larger Himalayas)</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 35.2px;">
<td style="width: 18.5594%;"><strong>Coordinates of Highest peak</strong></td>
<td style="width: 79.506%;">The summit is approximately 27&deg;59&prime;N latitude and 86&deg;9250&prime;E longitude</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 57.6px;">
<td style="width: 18.5594%;"><strong>Country Location of Mount Everest</strong></td>
<td style="width: 79.506%;">Border between Nepal and the Tibet Autonomous Region of China</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 35.2px;">
<td style="width: 18.5594%;"><strong>On the Border</strong></td>
<td style="width: 79.506%;">The peak of Mount Everest sits directly on the international border between the two countries</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 57.6px;">
<td style="width: 18.5594%;"><strong>Nepal Side (South)</strong></td>
<td style="width: 79.506%;">In Nepal, the mountain is in the Sagarmatha National Park, within the Solukhumbu District. The park is a UNESCO World Heritage site known for its rich biodiversity.</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 57.6px;">
<td style="width: 18.5594%;"><strong>China side (North)</strong></td>
<td style="width: 79.506%;">The northern face of Everest is in Tingri County, part of the Xigaz&ecirc; Prefecture in Tibet. This side is protected by the Qomolangma National Nature Preserve.&nbsp;</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 35.2px;">
<td style="width: 18.5594%;"><strong>Park</strong></td>
<td style="width: 79.506%;">Sagarmatha National Park of Nepal</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p><strong>Wondering where Mount Everest is or which country it belongs to</strong>? You&rsquo;re not alone thousands and millions of searches like "Where is Mount Everest located?", "Mount Everest in which country?", and "Mount Everest height" are among the most frequently asked questions online.</p>
<p><span style="background-color: #fbeeb8;">&nbsp;To clarify: <strong>Mount Everest is located on the border of Nepal and the Tibet Autonomous Region of China</strong>, </span>with its most popular access route and southern face lying entirely within Nepal.</p>
<p>So if you're askin<span style="background-color: #fbeeb8;">g "<strong>What country is Mount Everest in?", the answer is Nepal and China.</strong></span></p>
<p>Known locally as Sagarmatha and standing at a breathtaking <strong>height of 8,848.86 meters and in kilometres is 8.84886 km (29,031.7 feet), Everest</strong> is more than just the world&rsquo;s tallest mountain it&rsquo;s a cultural icon, a natural wonder, and a dream for adventurers. In this blog about Mount Everest, we&rsquo;ll take you beyond just facts like "Everest height" or "Mt Everest country". We&rsquo;ll explore its location, meaning, significance, and how you can experience it up close right here in Nepal.</p>
<h2 id="where-is-mount-everest-located-nepal-india-china-or-pakistan">Where is Mount Everest located: Nepal, India, China, or Pakistan?</h2>
<p><strong>Which country owns Mount Everest? Everest Geographic Location</strong>: Mount Everest is located on the border between Nepal and the Tibet Autonomous Region of China, in the Mahalangur Himal sub-range of the Himalayas. <strong>Mount Everest is not located in India, and it is the truth</strong>.</p>
<p><strong>Geographic Range:&nbsp;</strong>Part of the Mahalangur Himal range, which is a sub-range of the larger Himalayas.</p>
<p><strong>Mount Everest Elevation</strong>: Mount Everest's official height, established by a joint Nepalese and Chinese measurement expedition, is 8,848.86 meters (29,031.7 feet).</p>
<p><strong>Difficulty</strong>: Mount Everest is considered a highly difficult climb due to extreme altitude, harsh weather conditions, and challenging terrain. The standard route, while technically not the most difficult, still poses significant dangers like altitude sickness, icefalls, and the risk of avalanches.</p>
<p><strong>Mount Everest History</strong>: The climbing history of Mount Everest is marked by a progression of attempts and successes, culminating in the first documented summit in 1953 by Edmund Hillary and Tenzing Norgay. Before this, there were numerous British expeditions, notably those in 1921, 1922, and 1924, attempting the North Ridge route. The 1924 expedition, involving George Mallory and Andrew Irvine, is shrouded in mystery regarding their potential summit, raising questions about whether they were the first to reach the top.</p>
<p><strong>Climbing Routes:</strong> Mount Everest has two main climbing routes: the South Col Route (Nepal South Base Camp) and the North Col Route (Tibet). The South Col Route, also known as the Southeast Ridge route, is the most popular and well-supported route. It starts from Nepal, passes through the Khumbu Icefall, and eventually reaches the summit via the Southeast Ridge. The North face, on the other hand, begins in Tibet and is considered more remote and wind-exposed.</p>
<p><strong>Weather:</strong> Subject to extreme cold, strong winds, and rapidly changing conditions. While challenging, it is often less consistently harsh or unpredictable than K2's weather.</p>
<p><strong>Fatality Rate:</strong> Lower than K2's fatality rate per attempt, but the sheer number of climbers means more absolute deaths have occurred.</p>
<p><strong>Who first touched Mt Everest, First Ascent of the tallest peak:</strong> The first successful, undisputed ascent of Mount Everest was achieved on May 29, 1953, by Sir Edmund Hillary and Tenzing Norgay, via the Southeast Ridge.</p>
<h2 style="text-align: center;" id="what-continent-is-mount-everest-in-localizao-do-monte-evereste---nepal-tibete">What continent is Mount Everest in? Localiza&ccedil;&atilde;o do monte evereste - Nepal-Tibete</h2>
<figure class="image"><img src="https://nht-api.nepalhikingteam.com/media/itinerary-gallery/media-96a76846-1760424734.jpg" alt="Mount Everest">
<figcaption>Mount Everest</figcaption>
</figure>
<h2 id="mount-everests-exact-location-where-is-mount-everest-located-in-the-world">Mount Everest's Exact Location | Where is mount everest Located in the world?</h2>
<p>Mount Everest has an official height of 8,848.86 meters (29,031.7 feet) above sea level.</p>
<p><strong>Mount Everest Height:</strong> Mount Everest stands at an extraordinary height of 8,848.86 meters (29,032 feet), securing its status as the<a href="https://www.nepalhikingteam.com/highest-mountains-in-the-world"> highest mountain on Earth.</a></p>
<p><strong>Mount Everest Location:&nbsp;</strong>Along the border of Nepal and Tibet (China), Everest is a magnificent component of the Mahalangur Himal, a sub-range of the Himalayas. It is a remarkable link between the two nations and their rich cultural heritage.</p>
<h2 style="text-align: center;" id="where-is-located-mount-everest-which-country-is-everest-in-nepal-or-tibet"><span style="font-size: 14pt;"><em><strong>Where is located Mount Everest? Which country is Everest in, Nepal or Tibet?</strong></em></span></h2>
<figure class="image"><img src="https://nht-api.nepalhikingteam.com/media/attachments/media-7f391a4c-1734407199.jpg" alt="Where is Mount Everest Located?">
<figcaption>Mt Everest Where is: Where are Mount Everest?</figcaption>
</figure>
<p><strong>Significance</strong></p>
<p><strong>Symbol of Achievement:</strong> Mount Everest attracts adventurers worldwide, a spirit of determination, and all are eager to tackle its challenging landscape and extreme heights; many flock around during the peak seasons.</p>
<p><strong>Spiritual Reverence:</strong> The local communities of the <a href="https://www.nepalhikingteam.com/everest-region-trek" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Everest region</a> revere the mountain as Sagarmatha, which in Nepal signifies the "Forehead of the Sky" and Chomolungma, "The Goddess Mother of the World" in Tibet. Both names are profound symbols that resonate with those living in its shadow.</p>
<h2 id="which-country-shares-mount-everest-border-is-it-nepal-and-tibet">Which country shares Mount everest border? Is it Nepal and Tibet?</h2>
<p>Mount Everest is located on the international border between Nepal (in the south) and the Tibet Autonomous Region of China (in the north). The exact summit sits directly on this dividing line, meaning both countries share the iconic peak.</p>
<p>The southern slope is situated in the Solukhumbu District of Nepal (part of the Sagarmatha National Park), while the northern slope falls under Tingri County in Tibet. Because of this shared geography, climbers can approach and summit the mountain from either the Nepal side or the China side.</p>
<h2 id="is-mount-everest-located-in-the-alps">Is Mount Everest located in the Alps?</h2>
<p>No, Mount Everest is located in the Himalayas in Asia, specifically on the international border between Nepal and the Tibet Autonomous Region of China.</p>
<p>The Alps, on the other hand, are a completely different mountain range located entirely in Europe.</p>
<p>Here are a few quick facts about Everest's geography:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Mountain Range:</strong> It is part of the Mahalangur Himal sub-range of the Great Himalayas.</li>
<li><strong>Location:</strong> The summit lies directly on the border, with the southern face in Nepal and the northern face in Tibet.</li>
<li><strong>Elevation: </strong>It is the highest peak on Earth at an official height of 8,848.86 meters.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="geographical-location-of-mount-everest-where-is-mt-everest-situated">Geographical Location of Mount Everest: Where is Mt Everest situated?</h2>
<p>Popularly known as the pinnacle of our planet, Mount Everest is precisely located at coordinates 27.9881&deg; N latitude and 86.9250&deg; E longitude. These precise figures establish it as a distinctive landmark in the majestic Himalayas' heart.</p>
<p><strong>Nepal-Tibet Border:</strong></p>
<p>Bordering <a href="https://www.nepalhikingteam.com/highest-mountains-of-nepal">Nepal- Mount Everest,</a> which lies on the international border between China and Nepal, symbolizes a glaring fusion of shared cultural legacy and ecological significance.</p>
<p><strong>Administrative Divisions:</strong></p>
<p><strong>In Nepal,</strong> ideally located within the Solukhumbu District, Mount Everest, a treasured part of Sagarmatha National Park, is popular for its remarkable biodiversity and breathtaking landscapes. This <a href="https://www.nepalhikingteam.com/world-heritage-sites-of-nepal" target="_blank" rel="noopener">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> holds an esteemed recognition all over the world.</p>
<h2 style="text-align: center;" id="mount-everest-is-known-worldwide-as-the-highest-mountain-on-earth-a-symbol-of-extreme-mountaineering-and-a-culturally-sacred-peak"><em><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Mount Everest is known worldwide as the highest mountain on Earth, a symbol of extreme mountaineering, and a culturally sacred peak.</span></em></h2>
<figure class="image"><img src="https://nht-api.nepalhikingteam.com/media/attachments/media-7b177a30-1730888958.jpg" alt="What is the height of Mount Everest">
<figcaption>Sunrise view of Mount Everest from Nepal Kala Patthar</figcaption>
</figure>
<p><strong>In Tibet (China):</strong> The northern face of Everest is found in Tingri County, part of the Xigaz&ecirc; Prefecture, renowned for its dramatic high-altitude plateaus and striking natural scenery.</p>
<p><strong>Himalayan Range: </strong>As a crown jewel of the Mahalangur Himal sub-range, Mount Everest is an integral component of the more extensive Himalayan mountain range.</p>
<p><strong>Himalayan Reach:</strong> This extensive mountain range extends across five countries: Nepal, Tibet (China), India, Bhutan, and Pakistanrendering it a remarkable international wonder and making it a truly international marvel for travelers around the globe.</p>
<p><strong>Surrounding Peaks</strong>: Impressive neighbors, which include Lhotse (8,516 meters), Makalu (8,485 meters), and Cho Oyu (8,188 meters), flank Mount Everest, each adding to the majestic skyline of this awe-inspiring region.</p>
<h2 id="what-mountain-range-is-mount-everest-in-is-it-a-part-of-the-himalayas">What mountain range is Mount everest in? Is it a part of the Himalayas?</h2>
<p>Mount Everest is located in the Himalayas mountain range. Specifically, it is situated in the Mahalangur Himal sub-range of the Himalayas, right on the international border between Nepal and the Tibet Autonomous Region of China.</p>
<h2 id="is-mount-everest-8848-or-8849">Is Mount Everest 8848 or 8849?&nbsp;</h2>
<p>Mount Everest is officially recognized as being 8,849 meters (29,032 feet) tall. In late 2020, Nepal and China conducted a joint survey and determined the exact height of the snow cap to be 8,848.86 meters (29,031.7 feet). This precise figure is typically rounded up to 8,849 meters in modern records and geographical resources.</p>
<h2 id="historical-and-cultural-significance-everest-chomolungma">Historical and Cultural Significance: Everest Chomolungma​&nbsp;</h2>
<p>The significance of Mount Everest is far beyond its national geographical stature, and it's more about the embodied rich cultural and spiritual meanings that are reflected in its local names:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Nepali:</strong> Known as Sagarmatha, which translates to "Forehead of the Sky," this name highlights the mountain's majestic height and its celestial associations.</li>
<li><strong>Tibetan:</strong> Referred to as Chomolungma, or "Goddess Mother of the World," it captures the mountain's revered status among the Tibetan people.</li>
<li><strong>Naming History: </strong>The Western designation of Mount Everest emerged during the 19th-century Great Trigonometric Survey of India.</li>
<li><strong>Original Designation:</strong> "Peak XV" was formally identified as the tallest mountain in the world in 1852, a meticulous trigonometric calculation conducted by Indian mathematician Radhanath Sikdar.</li>
<li><strong>Renaming</strong>: In 1865, the Royal Geographical Society honored Sir George Everest, a British Surveyor General of India, with the mountain's current name. Sir George, who is said to have disapproved of the conferred tribute.</li>
<li>Although Mount Everest transcends its status as a geographical wonder, it is a profound spiritual symbol for the indigenous communities.</li>
<li><strong>Hinduism:</strong> The Nepalese Hindu community sees Sagarmatha as a sacred mountain. They believe its magnificent peaks connect them to the divine. Before setting out on journeys, the climbers and trekkers perform regular rituals and make offerings to ensure their safety.</li>
<li><strong>Buddhism:</strong> The name Chomolungma is held in high esteem by Tibetan Buddhists. They pay homage to the divine spirits believed to dwell there.</li>
</ul>
<h2 style="text-align: center;" id="berg-everest-where-exactly-is-mount-everest-located-what-country-is-everest-in"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><em><strong>Berg Everest: Where exactly is Mount Everest located? What country is Everest in?</strong></em></span></h2>
<figure class="image"><img src="https://nht-api.nepalhikingteam.com/media/attachments/media-31057790-1754282118.jpg" alt="Highest 5  Mount Everest The Top In The List">
<figcaption>Where to find Mount Everest? Which Country? Which Continent?</figcaption>
</figure>
<h2 id="geological-and-physical-features-of-berg-everest">Geological and Physical Features of Berg Everest</h2>
<p>Mount Everest is a powerful reminder of the Earth's ever-changing geological history.</p>
<p><strong>Tectonic Collision:</strong> The mountain was formed by the ongoing collision of the Indian Plate and the Eurasian Plate, a process that began about 60 million years ago during the Paleogene period.</p>
<p><strong>Growth Over Time:</strong> With an average rate of 4 millimeters every year, Mount Everest, the highest peak, continues to rise due to the persistent movement of these tectonic plates.</p>
<h2 id="geological-composition">Geological Composition</h2>
<p>Everest has an interesting story about its geological composition; however, the physical structure of Mount Everest depicts its intricate geological heritage, which has evolved.</p>
<h2 style="text-align: center;" id="mount-everest-is-located-on-the-border-between-nepal-and-the-tibet-autonomous-region-of-china-in-the-mahalangur-himal-sub-range-of-the-himalayas"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><em>Mount Everest is located on the border between Nepal and the Tibet Autonomous Region of China, in the Mahalangur Himal sub-range of the Himalayas.</em></span></h2>
<figure class="image"><img src="https://nht-api.nepalhikingteam.com/media/attachments/media-c128c7b8-1734414844.jpg" alt="Rock formation">
<figcaption>Geological Composition of the Mount Everest</figcaption>
</figure>
<p><strong>Rock Types</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Sedimentary Rocks:</strong> The combination of ancient marine limestone and shale layers of rocks found in the mountainous region are remnants of the long-vanished prehistoric Tethys Ocean that existed from the end of the Paleozoic era until the Cenozoic era.</li>
<li><strong>Metamorphic Rocks:</strong> The lower regions of Mount Everest consist of schists and gneisses, which were formed through significant heat and pressure. These lower areas are distinguished by schists and gneisses, developed under extreme heat and pressure conditions.</li>
<li><strong>Yellow Band: </strong>This distinctive layer of marbled limestone, visible just below the summit, is a notable marker for climbers and geologists.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Topography</strong></p>
<p>The topography of Everest is inexpressible because of its rugged topography, steep ridges, valleys, massive ice glaciers, and the surrounding mountains, which spellbind the climbers and the tourists.</p>
<p><strong>Ridges:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Southeast Ridge:</strong> A ridge popular because of the climbing route, traversing the Khumbu Icefall and climbing up to the South Col. between Mount Everest and Lhotse.</li>
<li><strong>Northeast Ridge:</strong> The Northeast Ridge, a desired route for ascent from Tibet for experienced climbers, features the demanding Second Step, a challenging pitch between 28,140 and 28,300 ft.</li>
<li><strong>West Ridge: </strong>This route is used less frequently and poses considerable technical challenges for trekkers.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Glaciers</strong>:</p>
<p>The icy glaciers of the Everest region, along with its surrounding landscape, are no wonder a stunning site to capture climbers. Still, they also make it challenging to ascend to higher altitudes.</p>
<h3 style="text-align: center;" id="where-is-mount-everest-in-asia-nepal-or-tibet"><em><strong>Where is Mount Everest in Asia? Nepal, or Tibet</strong></em></h3>
<figure class="image"><img src="https://nht-api.nepalhikingteam.com/media/attachments/media-80dd1486-1734415724.jpg" alt="Glaciers In The Everest Region   Ngozumpa Glacier">
<figcaption>Glaciers of Everest region</figcaption>
</figure>
<ul>
<li><strong>Khumbu Glacier: </strong>Found on the southern slope of Mount Everest, this glacier supplies water to the Dudh Kosi River.</li>
<li><strong>Rongbuk Glacier:</strong> Positioned on the northern flank, it channels water into the Rong River.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Icefalls:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Khumbu Icefall:</strong> Renowned for its large crevasses and ever-shifting ice, this section is one of the most dangerous for climbers.</li>
<li><strong>Western Cwm (Valley of Silence):</strong> A U-shaped glacial valley flanked by towering walls offers a quieter yet demanding part of the southern route.</li>
</ul>
<h2 style="text-align: center;" id="mount-everest-dimension-mt-everest-elevation-884886m-height-in-m"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><em><strong>Mount Everest Dimension: Mt Everest Elevation: 8848.86m (Height in m)</strong></em></span></h2>
<figure class="image"><img src="https://nht-api.nepalhikingteam.com/media/attachments/media-7cacc234-1734415724.jpg" alt="Where is Mount everest">
<figcaption>Gunung Everest: Mount Everest where?</figcaption>
</figure>
<h2 id="the-height-of-mount-everest-how-high-is-mt-everest">The Height of Mount Everest: How high is Mt Everest?</h2>
<p><strong>Height Evolution: </strong>The height has been revised over time due to technological advancements and the geological changes in the mountains.</p>
<p><strong>1852:</strong> The Great Trigonometric Survey of India first determined Everest's height at 8,848 meters (29,029 feet), which has been accepted for over a century.</p>
<p><strong>2020:</strong> A collaborative effort by Nepal and China established a revision of Mount Everest's new height of 8,848.86 meters (29,032 feet). The newly updated measurement of the mighty mountain considers variables such as snow cover and the thickness of the ice cap to improve accuracy.</p>
<h2 style="text-align: center;" id="mount-everest-height-in-feet-290317-feet"><span style="font-size: 14pt;"><strong><em>Mount Everest Height in feet: 29,031.7 feet</em></strong></span></h2>
<figure class="image"><img src="https://nht-api.nepalhikingteam.com/media/attachments/media-67062ca2-1734415006.jpg" alt="What is the height of mount everest">
<figcaption>Mt Everest Height: 8848.86m</figcaption>
</figure>
